  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad &#xf6;versyn/kontrol av skogsresurserna, WWF</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved forestry governance, WWF - Strengthened participation in the forest governanc</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det fyra &#xe5;r l&#xe5;nga projektet avs&#xe5;g att st&#xe4;rka civilsamh&#xe4;llets tekniska kapacitet att driva p&#xe5;verkansarbete och utkr&#xe4;va ansvar f&#xf6;r och f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndring av styrningen av skogssektorn, samt att &#xf6;ka allm&#xe4;nhetens kunskap om de milj&#xf6;m&#xe4;ssiga och ekonomiska konsekvenserna av den r&#xe5;dande situationen i Mo&#xe7;ambiques skogssektor. F&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; detta engagerades s&#xe5;v&#xe4;l lokalbefolkningar som civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer, media, privat sektor och offentliga institutioner i mediakampanjer, utbildningar och tv&#xe4;rsektoriell dialog ang&#xe5;ende skogssektorn. Projektet var nationellt, men med s&#xe4;rskilt fokus p&#xe5; de provinser som &#xe4;r rikast p&#xe5; produktiv skog och/eller h&#xe5;rdast drabbade av illegal skogssk&#xf6;vling, n&#xe4;mligen Sofala, Zamb&#xe9;zia, Tete, Nampula och Cabo Delgado.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The four-year long project aimed to strengthen the technical capacity of civil society to engage in advocacy, accountability and governance change in the forest sector, and to raise public awareness of the environmental and economic consequences of the current situation in the Mozambique forest sector. To achieve this, local populations as well as civil society organisations, the media, the private sector and public institutions were involved in media campaigns, training and cross-sectoral dialogue on the forest sector. The project was national, but with a particular focus on the provinces richest in productive forests and/or most affected by illegal deforestation, namely Sofala, Zamb&#xe9;zia, Tete, Nampula and Cabo Delgado.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forest Governance  the Urgency of the Moment, was a WWF project aiming to contribute to good governance in the forest sector by promoting participation and engagement of CSOs, the media and local communities and other key actors in a multi-stakeholder dialogue to improve the current status of forest governance in Mozambique. The project objective was to strengthen CSOs and local communities involvement in forest decision making and governance. 

The project had 2 specific objectives (medium term outcomes): 

Outcome 1. Civil society become key actors in influencing planning, decision-making and good governance of forest resources

Outcome 2. Communities increase influence in forest management decision making process and improve benefit sharing.

The project was implemented through the four CSO partners AAAJC, ADEL Sofala, Forum Terra Nampula and RADEZA.</narrative>
  </description>
